{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>They utter, they speak</b> — a root [meaning] arrogant speech." "<b>They exalt themselves</b> — they raise themselves up, as in: אֶת ה' הֶאֱמַרְתָּ (Deuteronomy 26:17), the meaning being the high branch, which is the lofty bough."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 94, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:37:08.913106764Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}